{"duration_api_ms":152046,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"ccbc877a-9875-4a48-947d-0ddeecc8c7d5","total_cost_usd":1.856553,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63719,"cache_read_input_tokens":3653,"output_tokens":11570,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7562},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63719,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11570,"cache_read_input_tokens":3653,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63719},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11570,"cacheReadInputTokens":3653,"cacheCreationInputTokens":63719,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.856553,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7562,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"schema\":\"agent-ee.review/1\",\"candidate_id\":\"7b6d5a949427df9a9100abf2208581f5564cf9ec758e1b0f1fbe731ff3a60283\",\"run_id\":\"c2a8c4b2-b486-46d7-a4ff-fd3cc013debf\",\"packet_sha256\":\"00ffb777086df1912dcdaf62ba9987e185048652f1742d94496eb5e3fa0ffe7c\",\"role\":\"independent initial engineering reviewer (physical/PCB)\",\"coverage\":[\"Re-derived J1/R1/C1 pin positions and wire/label connectivity from the native schematic (including the 180-degree rotation of J1) and confirmed the exported netlist (/IN: J1.1,R1.1; /OUT: J1.2,R1.2,C1.1; GND: J1.3,C1.2) matches it.\",\"Recomputed all pad coordinates from footprint placements in the native board file and traced every track segment endpoint: all land on correct-net pads or same-net copper, including the /OUT stub tee at (107.5,100); consistent with DRC 0 unconnected items.\",\"Independently confirmed all 5 track segments are written (width 0.25) in the native board file, satisfying the declared 0.20 mm minimum without relying on the geometry probe output.\",\"Inspected the saved B.Cu GND zone filled_polygon: clearance cutouts around J1.1 (/IN) and J1.2 (/OUT) with no spokes, and a 4-spoke thermal connection around J1.3 (GND) at (100,105.08), so the GND return path C1.2 -> track -> via (113,100) -> zone -> J1.3 is complete as saved.\",\"Checked placement/manufacturing basics: board outline 20x12 mm on Edge.Cuts, all pads, courtyards and the via inside the outline with margin; zone boundary 0.5 mm inside the edge.\",\"Verified simulation deck element values against schematic (R1=10k, C1=100n, tau=1 ms), checked node mapping and J1 exclusion, and recomputed expected step response: 1-exp(-1)=0.63212 vs measured 0.6321201 (within 0.62-0.65) and 1-exp(-5)=0.99326 vs measured 0.9932621.\",\"Cross-checked record consistency: board sha256 f8264d... identical across the packet artifact, DRC and geometry checks; ERC/DRC/netlist console logs consistent with their JSON reports; assessed stimulus adequacy (1 ns PWL rise contributes ~1e-6 relative error at 1 ms, negligible).\"],\"limitations\":[\"I could not re-run any tool; all tool outputs were verified only by cross-reading against the native source files supplied in the packet.\",\"work/rc-step/result.raw is binary and retained for the operator; I verified the two .meas values from ngspice.log and independent arithmetic, not from the raw waveform.\",\"Zone fill was evaluated as saved; thermal spoke presence and widths around J1.3 were judged by inspecting the saved filled_polygon vertices, not by an independent refill.\",\"No current, ampacity, thermal, tolerance, loading, EMI or ADC-sampling requirements are declared for this fixture, so none were evaluated; the single-via GND return is therefore noted only as an untested shared path, not judged against any rating.\",\"ERC/DRC ran with several checks ignored (e.g. single_global_label, missing_courtyard); I did not attempt to reconstruct what those checks would have reported.\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"F1\",\"title\":\"Geometry probe emitted native pcbnew assertion failures while reporting success\",\"location\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"condition\":\"The geometry probe exited 0 and the check passed, but its console shows repeated native assertions: three PROPERTY_ENUM 'No enum choices defined' failures and 'PCB_VIA::GetWidth called without a layer argument' (pcb_track.cpp:387).\",\"mechanism\":\"Assertion failures inside the pcbnew API indicate the probe is exercising code paths the library considers invalid (notably via width retrieval); a future or edge-case board could yield wrong or missing width data while the probe still exits successfully, so a successful exit alone does not prove the measurement path is sound.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"locator\":\"lines containing 'assert \\\"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\\\"' and 'PCB_VIA::GetWidth called without a layer argument'\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"five (segment ... (width 0.25)) entries and (via (at 113 100) (size 0.6) (drill 0.3))\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[] width_mm values, all 0.25; via entry width_mm 0.6\"}],\"reasoning\":\"For this board the result is independently corroborated: all five segments are written width 0.25 in the native board file and the via (0.6 mm) is not a track segment under the declared requirement, so the pass verdict stands. The concern is tool health/reliability of the record, not the board.\"},{\"id\":\"F2\",\"title\":\"vout_5ms measurement has no acceptance limits and cannot fail\",\"location\":\"work/rc-step (criterion rc-step, measurement vout_5ms)\",\"condition\":\"The declared rc-step criterion includes a 5 ms measurement with no min or max; the check records measured 0.9932621 with min/max null and still contributes to an overall 'pass'.\",\"mechanism\":\"A limitless measurement provides no discrimination: any value, including one indicating a wrong C or R, would not fail the check at 5 ms, so verification coverage of the settled response rests entirely on the single 1 ms point.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/ngspice.log\",\"locator\":\"'vout_5ms            =  9.932621e-01'\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/deck.cir\",\"locator\":\"'.meas tran vout_5ms FIND v(OUT) AT=5m'\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"requirement 1 (only the 1 ms window 0.62-0.65 V is specified)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The declared requirements only bound the 1 ms point, so this is not a violation; I independently confirmed 0.9932621 matches 1-exp(-5)=0.99326 for the intended RC. Noting it because an unbounded measurement in the pass/fail record can be mistaken for additional verified coverage.\"},{\"id\":\"F3\",\"title\":\"GND return is a single untested chokepoint: one 0.25 mm track, one 0.3 mm-drill via, and zone thermal spokes\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb (GND net routing)\",\"condition\":\"The only conductive path from C1 pad 2 to J1 pin 3 is: 2.05 mm of 0.25 mm F.Cu track to a single via (0.6 mm pad, 0.3 mm drill) at (113,100), through the B.Cu GND zone, then into J1.3 solely via ~0.5 mm thermal bridges (zone thermal_bridge_width 0.5).\",\"mechanism\":\"Every GND return current shares one via and the thermal spokes; none of the declared checks exercise current, impedance or thermal behavior of this path, and the transient check uses an ideal netlist that cannot see layout parasitics, so the electrical adequacy of this return is entirely unverified.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"(segment (start 110.95 100) (end 113 100) (width 0.25) (net GND)); (via (at 113 100) (size 0.6) (drill 0.3) (net GND)); zone (net GND) (thermal_bridge_width 0.5) with spoke geometry around (100,105.08) in filled_polygon\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"scope limits paragraph (no current/thermal requirement declared)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[] GND entry and via entry; zones[0] net GND, filled true\"}],\"reasoning\":\"No current or thermal requirement is declared for this disposable fixture, so this is not a defect, and for the microamp-scale signals implied by a 10 k/100 n filter the path is almost certainly adequate. I flag it because it is the one shared current/return path on the board and no criterion, simulated or geometric, challenges it; per my role I do not infer ampacity from the saved widths.\"}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"7b6d5a949427df9a9100abf2208581f5564cf9ec758e1b0f1fbe731ff3a60283","run_id":"c2a8c4b2-b486-46d7-a4ff-fd3cc013debf","packet_sha256":"00ffb777086df1912dcdaf62ba9987e185048652f1742d94496eb5e3fa0ffe7c","role":"independent initial engineering reviewer (physical/PCB)","coverage":["Re-derived J1/R1/C1 pin positions and wire/label connectivity from the native schematic (including the 180-degree rotation of J1) and confirmed the exported netlist (/IN: J1.1,R1.1; /OUT: J1.2,R1.2,C1.1; GND: J1.3,C1.2) matches it.","Recomputed all pad coordinates from footprint placements in the native board file and traced every track segment endpoint: all land on correct-net 